  "rationale": "Long-term screen: AD-bMSC-Cas9 pre-cultured ~75 days, then transduced at high MOI with the same 3,000-guide library as GSE280676 (2,564 guides on 603 genes, 436 nc_guide non-cutting controls, each with its own label), 3 replicate cultures sampled from day 1 to day 100. The counts file is the GEO UTF-16 table converted unchanged to UTF-8; column names match GSM titles. Day 15 is the last time point before clonal takeover (top 1% of guides hold 16-19% of reads; 28-35% at day 20, 66-72% at day 30, >92% from day 50), so the primary contrast is day 15 vs day 1 with library totals, with median-ratio totals as a sensitivity run, day 10 vs day 1 as an earlier, cleaner but weaker contrast, and day 30 vs day 1 (median-ratio totals, enrichment only) to document clonal takeover. Because cells carry several guides (high MOI), passenger guides co-inherited with a driver guide rise with it; gene calls supported by one guide must be read with that in mind. No replicate term: day-1 replicates are indistinguishable.",
  "counts_md5": "76b99bcf2a3beba82c923ba2d756dcd9"
